PROBLEM="Write an async method that callers can await and that surfaces exceptions correctly."
LEARNINGS="An async method MUST return Task (or Task<T> / ValueTask), never 'async void'. Task is awaitable and observable: the caller can await completion and catch exceptions. 'async void' is fire-and-forget - the caller cannot await it and any thrown exception crashes the process instead of propagating."
ERRORS="Do NOT use 'async void' for anything except an event handler. async void cannot be awaited and its exceptions are unobservable (they tear down the process)."
TAGS="src:context7 lang:csharp area:async"
REF_SRC="Worker.cs"
